.TH LBCTL 1 "lbctl 0.1.0" "Sep 2026" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lbctl \- Gracefully disable an F5 BIG-IP pool member for maintenance.

.SYNOPSIS
.B lbctl
.I [global options]
.IC command

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Gracefully disable an F5 BIG-IP pool member for maintenance.
.PP
Flow for `disable`: 1. Set the member's session to \(dquser-disabled\(sd
(it leaves load-balancing rotation; the health monitor no longer governs
it, so no monitor \(dqfailure\(sd is generated while the node comes
out). 2. Wait for active connections to drain to zero (configurable
timeout).
.PP
`enable` flips the session state back (\(dquser-enabled\(sd) to bring a
node back into service. `disable` also covers a quick drain (with
\&--max-wait 0), where you just want to pull a node out of rotation
without waiting. `status` reports current state for one member
(--member) or, if --member is omitted, every member in the pool.
.PP
`list-partitions`, `list-pools`, and `list-members` are read-only
discovery commands: they list the administrative partitions, pools, and
pool members visible with the configured credentials, so you can find
the exact `--partition`/`--pool`/`--member` values to target before
running `status`/`disable`/`enable`.
.PP
`--member`/`-m` accepts either the member's IP address or its BIG-IP
node name -- pool members are often created against a named node rather
than a raw IP, so this lets you target one the same way you'd refer to
it in the F5 UI, without having to look up its IP or port first. A port
is only needed (as `name:port`) if a pool happens to have the same
node/IP on more than one port.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.B --host, -H
BIG-IP management hostname/IP (CLI > config > F5_URL)
.B --user, -u
BIG-IP username (CLI > config > F5_USER)
.B --password
BIG-IP password (CLI > config > F5_PASSWORD). Avoid argv for security.
.B -c, --config
TOML (or .json) config file with connection defaults (default:
$LBCTL_CONFIG or ~/.lbctl.toml)
.B -i, --init-config
Create the config file (with a template) if it does not exist, then exit
.B --no-verify
Skip TLS certificate verification (self-signed certs). Also settable in
the config file as insecure = true
.B --verbose, -v
Log every REST call (method, path, response status/timing) to stderr
.B --partition, -p
Partition containing the pool and member (default: common)
.B --pool, -P
Pool name (required)
.B --member, -m
Member node IP address or BIG-IP node name. Required for disable/enable;
optional for status (omit to list every member in the pool)
.B --version
show program's version number and exit

