.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check one member's state (name or IP works for --member):
.RS
\&.B lbctl --pool web_pool --member web03.example.com status
.RE
.PP
List every member in a pool so you can pick one to target:
.RS
\&.B lbctl --pool web_pool list-members
.RE
.PP
Disable a member and keep it (no prompt, no wait):
.RS
\&.B lbctl --pool web_pool --member 10.1.2.3 --disable
.RE
.PP
Bring a previously disabled member back into rotation:
.RS
\&.B lbctl --pool web_pool --member web03.example.com --enable
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.lbctl.toml
Connection defaults (password included). The tool refuses to load it unless it is mode 600.

